    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.breadcrumbs\n\n### Description\n\nIs there any plan on adding something like [nvim-navic](https://github.com/SmiteshP/nvim-navic) to the mini.nvim suite of plugins. For getting breadcrumbs we can leverage treesitter or lsp as nvim-navic does or use nvim_treesitter#statusline() to get the current context and parse it accordingly into proper format.",
