            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "+1 on breadcrumbs\n\nMany people don't use tabs, and the breadcrumbs are awesome in big files with a lot of nesting. \n\nI've been using this guy these past few years: [barbecue.nvim](https://github.com/utilyre/barbecue.nvim) — it's awesome and gets the job done — but it's an archived wrapper around navic, and I wouldn't mind removing one more plugin in favor of a well-thought-out mini module.\n\nI don't have much to add to the above discussion, if I were to implement it myself, I would most likely succumb to treesitter.\n\nAppreciate you.",
